cfg_packedexp -- C6: packed half-precision exponential (thu-ml/SageAttention @ d1a57a5)

Contains all of cfg_base.patch unchanged (h2_tiles.h tile macros, the seven sm89_*.cu launchers,
pybind_sm89.cpp h2_tile_config(), core.py tile/V-pad derivation, setup.py env-var overrides), so
build.sh and bench.py work exactly as for the other cfgs:
    bash bench/attn/h2_tiles/build.sh cfg_packedexp
    /workspace/sage_h2/venv_cfg_packedexp/bin/python bench/attn/h2_tiles/bench.py --cfg cfg_packedexp
Tiles stay at upstream 128/64/32/64.

WHAT CHANGES
  csrc/qattn/attn_utils.cuh, update_mdo(): the four scalar
      RS[fq][fk][k*2 + {0,1,4,5}] = math::ptx_exp2(fmaf(RS, sm_scale, negative_m))
  per (fragment, row-half) become two packed calls on the adjacent pairs {0,1} and {4,5}:
      half2 e = math::ptx_exp2(__floats2half2_rn(x_a, x_b));   // ex2.approx.f16x2
      RS[..a] = __low2float(e);  RS[..b] = __high2float(e);
  math::ptx_exp2(half2) already exists in csrc/math.cuh (lines 59-68) and was dead code at d1a57a5 --
  nothing called it. FlashInfer uses the same instruction in its FP16-QK prefill path
  (include/flashinfer/attention/prefill.cuh ~L1805-1843); as far as we know nobody does it in an
  FP8/INT8 kernel. One ex2.approx.f16x2 computes two exponentials in one SFU/MUFU slot, so the
  softmax's transcendental issue slots per row-half per warp drop from 16 to 8.
  RS keeps its fp32 storage type: accumulate_d (row sum d) and RS_32_to_8 (the e4m3 P conversion)
  both read fp32, so only the exponential itself is packed.
  o_scale = ptx_exp2(m_prev - m) is left scalar: one per row per K tile (1/16 of the exp2 traffic),
  and it is not adjacent to anything packable.

PRECISION -- NOT BIT-IDENTICAL, on purpose
  fp16 has 10 stored mantissa bits vs fp32's 23, so P now carries ~3 decimal digits before the e4m3
  conversion (which itself keeps 3 mantissa bits). Range is not the issue:
    * argument x = S*sm_scale - m <= S_FP8_OFFSET = 8.807 (m carries the -S_FP8_OFFSET offset) and
      >= about -20 in practice;  result P = 2^x in [0, 448].
    * fp16 spans [6.1e-5 min normal .. 65504 max]: 448 is 146x below the top, and e4m3's smallest
      representable magnitude (min subnormal 2^-9 = 1.95e-3) is 32x ABOVE fp16's min normal, i.e.
      every P the very next step can represent at all is a normal fp16. No overflow, no flush.
  The error is a rounding error, twice:
    * argument rounded to fp16 first: near |x| = 8.8 the fp16 ulp is 2^3 * 2^-10 = 7.8e-3, half-ulp
      3.9e-3, so relative error in P of 2^0.0039 - 1 = 0.27%. Near x = -20 it is 0.54%, but those P
      are ~1e-6 and carry no weight in the row.
    * result rounded to fp16: 2^-11 = 0.05% relative.
  Both are small next to the e4m3 conversion immediately downstream (3 stored mantissa bits ->
  6.25% half-ulp relative quantisation, ~128x coarser), and d is accumulated from the same perturbed
  P, so numerator and denominator move together. Expected cosine effect: small but nonzero.
  bench.py measures cosine against an fp32 SDPA reference; ACCEPTANCE GATE is
  cosine >= the baseline's 0.999246 (and no spill stores in build.sh's cuobjdump output).

TWO MACROS (both live in csrc/qattn/h2_tiles.h)
  SAGE_H2_PACKED_EXP      default 1 -- the variant described above (fp32 argument, packed exp only).
                          Build the scalar control from the same source with
                          NVCC_APPEND_FLAGS="-DSAGE_H2_PACKED_EXP=0" (that is byte-identical to
                          cfg_base's kernel).
  SAGE_H2_PACKED_EXP_ARG  default 0 -- the fully packed variant: the fmaf is also done in half2
                          (__hfma2 / __hadd2), so the whole exp path is packed and 2 FFMA + 1
                          cvt.rn.f16x2.f32 per pair collapse to 1 cvt + 1 HFMA2. Enable with
                          NVCC_APPEND_FLAGS="-DSAGE_H2_PACKED_EXP_ARG=1".
                          RISK, stronger than "less precise": all three update_mdo call sites in
                          qk_int_sv_f8_cuda_sm89.cuh pass fuse_scale = false, so RS here is the RAW
                          int8 QK accumulator turned into float (__int2float_rz), bounded only by
                          head_dim * 127 * 127 = 2.06e6. Converting that to fp16 BEFORE applying
                          sm_scale overflows to +-inf whenever a row's peak accumulator exceeds
                          65504, and exp2(+inf) = inf poisons the tile. So this variant is correct
                          only on data whose int8 QK accumulators stay under 65504; bench it as an
                          upper bound on what packing can save and let the cosine check reject it.
                          Making it safe would mean folding a power-of-two shrink into the
                          __int2float_rz in qk_int_sv_f8_cuda_sm89.cuh -- out of scope here.

VERIFICATION DONE (CPU only, no GPU)
  * source tree checked byte-identical to d1a57a5 before editing; patch generated with `git diff`.
  * `git apply --check` (no --recount) clean on a fresh d1a57a5 checkout.
  * update_mdo extracted into a stub TU and syntax-checked with clang++ -std=c++17 -fsyntax-only for
    all three settings (packed default / PACKED_EXP_ARG=1 / PACKED_EXP=0) and for both DTypeSVAccum
    instantiations (float and half). Not compiled by nvcc -- that happens on the pod.

